# ig-wrapped

## Stack

- **Backend:** Node.js (ESM), Express 4, Multer, CORS (optional; not used by shipped UI).
- **Frontend:** React 18, Vite 5, **fflate** (client-side ZIP unzip).
- **Language:** JavaScript only (no TypeScript in this repo).

## Run (local)

- **Backend (optional):** `cd backend` → `npm install` → `npm run dev` → `http://localhost:4000`
- **Frontend:** `cd frontend` → `npm install` → `npm run dev` → `http://localhost:5173` (opens **Wrapped**; `/` redirects to `/wrapped`)

## Hosting

- **Frontend:** Vercel — static Vite build. Root directory **`frontend`**, framework preset Vite, output `dist`.
- **Backend:** Render Web Service (optional) — Root directory **`backend`**, start command `npm start`, listens on `process.env.PORT || 4000`.
- **`VITE_API_URL`** — only needed if re-enabling the legacy Non-Followers upload flow; baked in at **build time** on Vercel.
- **`frontend/vercel.json`** — SPA catch-all rewrite so `/wrapped`, `/guide`, and refresh on deep links work.
- **`.github/workflows/frontend-ci.yml`** — runs `npm ci && npm run build` on PRs touching `frontend/**`.

## Shipped product (UI)

- **Only two routes** in [`App.jsx`](frontend/src/App.jsx): **`/wrapped`** (default) and **`/guide`** (export instructions). [`resolveRoute`](frontend/src/config/features.js) maps `/` and all legacy paths (`/heatmap`, `/`, etc.) to **`/wrapped`**.
- **Nav:** Wrapped | How to export | Data loaded / Clear.
- **Export ingest:** [`ExportPicker.jsx`](frontend/src/components/ExportPicker.jsx) — **Choose ZIP** or **Choose folder** → [`normalizeExportInput`](frontend/src/utils/exportIngest.js) in [`ExportDataContext.jsx`](frontend/src/context/ExportDataContext.jsx). ZIP path extracts **JSON only** via fflate; folder path uses `webkitdirectory`. Validates paths containing `your_instagram_activity/` or `personal_information/`.
- **Export guide:** [`ExportGuide.jsx`](frontend/src/components/ExportGuide.jsx) — Phone vs desktop steps; recommends Instagram export date range **about 6 months to 1 year** (JSON, export to device).
- **Privacy:** Wrapped does **not** upload the export; parsing runs in the browser.

## Folder map

- **`backend/src/`** — `server.js`, `app.js`; `routes/upload.js`; `services/compareUsers.js`; `parsers/instagramParsers.js`; `middleware/errorHandler.js`
- **`frontend/src/`**
  - **`App.jsx`** — Wrapped + guide only
  - **`config/features.js`** — route resolution
  - **`context/ExportDataContext.jsx`** — `files`, `loadExport`, ingest loading/error state, parser caches for Wrapped
  - **`components/`** — `ExportPicker.jsx`, `ExportGuide.jsx`, `WrappedSlideChrome.jsx`, `WrappedAvatarPodium.jsx`; `FolderPicker.jsx` (alias → ExportPicker)
  - **`pages/`** — `WrappedPage.jsx`, `wrappedSlideContent.jsx`, `GuidePage.jsx`; legacy `HeatmapPage`, `SocialGraphPage`, `MessagesPage`, `MostUsedWordsPage` (not routed)
  - **`utils/`** — `exportIngest.js`, `wrappedData.js`, `wrappedPalette.js`, `wrappedThemes.js`, `wrappedAvatars.js`, `profileSearches.js`, plus shared parsers (`commentHeatmap.js`, `socialInteractionGraph.js`, `messageFrequency.js`, `mostUsedWords.js`)
  - **`styles.css`** — mobile nav, export guide/picker, Wrapped 9:16 story column
- **`frontend/.env.example`** — documents optional `VITE_API_URL`
- **`frontend/vercel.json`** — SPA rewrite
- **`docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md`** — rolling handoff for AI/contributors

## API (backend, optional)

- **`GET /health`** → `{ "ok": true }`
- **`POST /upload`** (`multipart/form-data`): `followersFile`, `followingFile` → `{ "non_followers": [...] }` (legacy Non-Followers; not exposed in current UI)

## Conventions

- Match existing style: focused diffs, no unrelated refactors.
- **Wrapped** (`/wrapped`) is client-only after export load: **ten 9:16 story cards** in a vertical scroller (scroll-snap, Prev/Next/dots/arrow keys, screenshot-friendly), light glass styling, per-slide accents (`wrappedThemes.js`), activity-style stack charts (`wrappedPalette.js`), body quips after charts, merged footer on data slides. Slide order: intro → span → activity → likes → comments → story interactions → DMs → profile searches → privacy → teaser. Orchestration: `wrappedData.js` (`loadWrappedBaseline`); reuses or fills `heatmapCache`, `socialGraphCache`, `messagesCache`.
- When extending Instagram export parsing, reuse patterns from **`commentHeatmap.js`** and align with **`socialInteractionGraph.js`** where overlap exists.
- No new heavy chart libraries unless explicitly approved.

## Optional scoped rules

Add separate `.mdc` files with `globs` (e.g. `frontend/**/*.jsx`, `backend/**/*.js`) if you need frontend-only or backend-only guidance beyond this file.
